151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (The project showed that maps are more useful when they include both science and local knowledge. Drone pictures can show where roads, rivers, homes, and coastlines are located, but residents can explain how those places are affected during real storms. A road may look safe on a map, but people nearby may know it floods after heavy rain. This shows why disaster planning should include the people who know the community best.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
